+| Concurrent visit edit handling | Whole-visit revisions | Field-aware three-way merge | The server cannot infer field relatedness from names, so any automatic field-disjointness merge is a standing guess that can silently combine scientifically related edits (e.g. a species ID and its cover estimate) with no review step to catch a wrong guess. Whole-visit revisions keep every exported value traceable to a submission a worker actually made, at the cost of review volume scaling with independent same-visit corrections. See [decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md](decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md). |
 
